  E=[1, 2, 60, 61, 4000]: level-1 err = +0.000000, proven C1/b1 = 20.832000, OK

CONCLUSION: the TV/IBP contraction holds with the PROVEN constants at every test;
the far-element plateau is now a THEOREM with explicit rate C(E')/b, C(E') = 
sum_T 2|T| * (sum E') * |T|(7-|T|)/14 over the 127 sector atoms (IE), i.e.
C(E') = (sum E') * sum_{t=1}^{7} C(7,t) * t^2 (7-t)/7  -- pure arithmetic.
